// =====================================================================
// SCENE 3 · DAY 2: MAKING SURE HE READS THEM
// Anin finds out the notes are real and makes sure Fal reads them,
// believing they'll help. He goes quiet, and he dies again in the
// evening. "But I... I helped him."
//
// NOTES FOR THE PROGRAMMER
// - Every "//" comment is a stage direction for you, not in-game text.
// - First day with full player agency: the player can explore anywhere.
//   Event triggers show as an exclamation mark on the minimap, and a
//   small pop-up appears before an event starts.
// - Commands used (same as earlier scenes, plus a few new ones):
//     <<enable_control>>              give the player movement + interact
//     <<quest_start "id" "Title">>    start / show a quest
//     <<quest_update "id" "Title">>   update the quest objective
//     <<scene_transition "Location">> fade + load a location
//     <<advance_time "slot">>         morning / after_school
//     <<event_marker "id" true/false>> show/hide minimap "!" for an event
//     <<npc_enter "Name">>            NPC walks into the current room
//     <<npc_exit "Name">>             NPC walks out
//     <<cutscene "id">>               play a non-dialogue cutscene
//     <<hard_reset>>                  white flash, loop back to the wish
// - World state from Gap 1: the notes are inside Fal's math textbook.
//   The ROOFTOP key is ON its hook in the morning, EMPTY after school.
// - The note text must NEVER be visible in this scene. The player only
//   sees the back of the paper, and later only the torn fragment.
// =====================================================================


// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// DORM — MORNING
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------

title: Day2_Start
tags: scene3 day2 dorm
---
// Lets the Dorm door run Day2_Dorm_Door instead of leaving freely.
<<set $story_exit to true>>
<<set $d2_dressed to false>>
<<set $d2_morning_examined to 0>>
<<set $d2_seen_locker to false>>
<<set $d2_seen_hook to false>>
<<set $d2_seen_cabinet to false>>
<<set $d2_fal_arrived to false>>
<<set $d2_eve_clock to false>>
<<set $d2_eve_hook to false>>
<<set $d2_found_paper to false>>
<<set $d2_paper_dropped to false>>

// Anin wakes up. This time Kirana IS there, still asleep.
// Anin tries to remember last night's "dream": wandering an empty
// school. The memory is faint. Only a few moments come back.
Anin: Wha— was it all just a dream?
Anin: Or did I actually get up and sleepwalk around school last night?
Anin: Why did it feel so real?
Anin: Did I really go to Fal's locker and find out all of that?
Anin: I dreamt I wrote him something. Something kind... I think. In his math book.
<<enable_control>>
<<quest_start "day2" "Get ready for school">>
// Interactables: Day2_Dorm_Bed, Day2_Dorm_Poster, Day2_Dorm_Desk,
// Day2_Dorm_KiranaBed, Day2_Dorm_Door
===

title: Day2_Dorm_Bed
tags: scene3 day2 dorm interactable
---
Anin: No time to lie around, Anin...
===

title: Day2_Dorm_Poster
tags: scene3 day2 dorm interactable
---
Anin: Kirana's favorite band. I don't really listen to this kind of music.
===

title: Day2_Dorm_Desk
tags: scene3 day2 dorm interactable
---
<<if $d2_dressed>>
    // Already dressed: the choice is gone, only this line plays.
    Anin: I'm already dressed. Time to go.
<<else>>
    Anin: I should hurry.
    -> Get dressed
        <<set $d2_dressed to true>>
        <<fade>>
        // Anin showers, rushes through her makeup, puts on her uniform.
        // Play a short fade or outfit swap here.
    -> Do nothing
<<endif>>
===

title: Day2_Dorm_KiranaBed
tags: scene3 day2 dorm interactable
---
Anin: Wake her up?
-> Yes
    Kirana: Ummmm... just five more minutes.
    Anin: Bruh. Is this what she went through yesterday?
-> Do nothing
===

title: Day2_Dorm_Door
tags: scene3 day2 dorm interactable
---
<<if $d2_dressed is false>>
    Anin: I can't go out like this.
<<else>>
    Anin: Leave the room?
    -> Yes
        <<jump Day2_FreeRoam>>
    -> Later
<<endif>>
===

title: Day2_FreeRoam
tags: scene3 day2
---
// Free exploration starts. Show the event marker on the minimap.
// These run BEFORE the transition: nothing after <<scene_transition>> runs.
<<quest_update "day2" "Explore the school">>
<<event_marker "day2_fal_notes" true>>
// Event: Day2_Lockers_Morning (trigger: enter the Locker Room).
// Optional day events will be added later.
<<scene_transition "LockerRoom">>
===


// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// EVENT: FINDING OUT WHETHER FAL READS THE NOTES
// Trigger: enter the Locker Room (morning). Show the event pop-up first.
// Interactables: Day2_Morning_FalLocker, Day2_Morning_KeyHook,
// Day2_Morning_Cabinet. Fal arrives after the player examines ANY TWO.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------

title: Day2_Lockers_Morning
tags: scene3 day2 lockers event
---
<<event_marker "day2_fal_notes" false>>
Anin: It looks exactly the same as in my dream. So... it wasn't a dream?
===

title: Day2_Morning_FalLocker
tags: scene3 day2 lockers interactable
---
Anin: Locked. Of course it is. But last night it was open... I opened it.
<<if $d2_seen_locker is false>>
    <<set $d2_seen_locker to true>>
    <<set $d2_morning_examined to $d2_morning_examined + 1>>
<<endif>>
<<jump Day2_Morning_Check>>
===

title: Day2_Morning_KeyHook
tags: scene3 day2 lockers interactable
---
// Hook tag: ROOFTOP. The key IS on the hook this morning.
Anin: The rooftop key's still here. Just like in my dream.
<<if $d2_seen_hook is false>>
    <<set $d2_seen_hook to true>>
    <<set $d2_morning_examined to $d2_morning_examined + 1>>
<<endif>>
<<jump Day2_Morning_Check>>
===

title: Day2_Morning_Cabinet
tags: scene3 day2 lockers interactable
---
Anin: I said sorry to him. In the dream, I said sorry.
<<if $d2_seen_cabinet is false>>
    <<set $d2_seen_cabinet to true>>
    <<set $d2_morning_examined to $d2_morning_examined + 1>>
<<endif>>
<<jump Day2_Morning_Check>>
===

title: Day2_Morning_Check
tags: scene3 day2 lockers
---
<<if $d2_morning_examined >= 2 and $d2_fal_arrived is false>>
    <<set $d2_fal_arrived to true>>
    <<jump Day2_FalReads>>
<<endif>>
===

title: Day2_FalReads
tags: scene3 day2 lockers event
---
// Footsteps. Fal comes in, bag over one shoulder, opens his locker.
<<npc_enter "Fal">>
Fal: Oh. Anin. You're early for once.
<<face_character "Anin" "left">>
<<close_dialogue_bubble>>
<<move_character_to_actor "Fal" "Anin" -2.5 10 "walk">>
Anin: Morning, Fal.
-> Did you bring your math book?
-> Let's start studying now, before class.
Fal: Now? Okay, okay, teacher.

<<cutscene "fal_reads_notes">>
// Fal pulls out his math textbook. Folded papers slip out and land at
// his feet. He picks them up and turns AWAY to read. Camera shows only
// the back of the paper. A long pause. His shoulders drop.
// NO MUSIC. Hold the silence for a few seconds before the next line.

Fal: What's...
Fal: ...Who wrote these?
-> Someone who believes in you.
-> Does it matter?
// Keep both options exactly as written. They pay off at the Day 3 midpoint.

// Fal folds the notes into his blazer pocket.
Fal: ...Right.
Fal: Thanks.
Fal: Let's just do the integrals after school. Lockers, like we said.
<<close_dialogue_bubble>>
<<move_character "Fal" 12.5 10 "walk">>
// He leaves without looking back.
<<npc_exit "Fal">>

Anin: He went quiet. That's good, right? It means it reached him.
<<quest_update "day2" "Meet Fal at the lockers after school">>
<<advance_time_teleport_character "after_school" "Anin" 28.0854 "left">>
// Optional day events will go here later. For now, time advances
// straight to after school once this event ends.
// Anin is still in the Locker Room, and a start node only plays when a
// room loads, so the evening starts here directly.
<<jump Day2_Lockers_Evening>>
===


// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// LOCKER ROOM — AFTER SCHOOL (required)
// Trigger: enter the Locker Room after the bell.
// Interactables: Day2_Eve_Clock, Day2_Eve_KeyHook.
// The ROOFTOP key hook is EMPTY now.
// Friends arrive after BOTH are examined.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------

title: Day2_Lockers_Evening
tags: scene3 day2 lockers
---
// Late sunlight through the high window. Anin waits beside Fal's
// locker, two math books under her arm.
Anin: Today's different. He read them. Today's different.
===

title: Day2_Eve_Clock
tags: scene3 day2 lockers interactable
---
Anin: Ten minutes late. ...Ten minutes, again.
<<set $d2_eve_clock to true>>
<<jump Day2_Eve_Check>>
===

title: Day2_Eve_KeyHook
tags: scene3 day2 lockers interactable
---
// Hook tag: ROOFTOP. The hook is EMPTY.
Anin: ...No. No, no, no.
<<set $d2_eve_hook to true>>
<<jump Day2_Eve_Check>>
===

title: Day2_Eve_Check
tags: scene3 day2 lockers
---
<<if $d2_eve_clock and $d2_eve_hook>>
    Anin: Please, not again.
    <<close_dialogue_bubble>>
    <<move_character "Anin" -15.8 10 "walk">>
    <<jump Day2_FriendsArrive>>
<<endif>>
===

title: Day2_FriendsArrive
tags: scene3 day2 lockers event
---
// Footsteps. Kirana, Dira and Lila come in from the hallway.
// Lila shoves her sketchbook into her locker.
<<npc_enter "Kirana">>
<<npc_enter "Lila">>
Lila: Anin? You're still here?
<<face_character "Anin" "right">>
<<close_dialogue_bubble>>
<<start_character_move "Lila" -11.6 10 "walk" 0>>
<<start_character_move "Kirana" -13.4 10 "walk" 0>>
<<wait_for_character_moves>>
Kirana: She's waiting for her study date.
Kirana: Don't stay too late, Sleeping Beauty. I'm not waking you up—
// Anin says "twice" AT THE SAME TIME as Kirana would. Show both
// speakers or overlap the boxes if your dialogue UI allows it.
// PAYOFF in Scene 7 lunch: Kirana says "You finish my sentences too."
Anin: —twice.
Kirana: ...Creepy. Okay. Bye.
<<close_dialogue_bubble>>
<<start_character_move "Lila" -32.6 10 "walk" 0>>
<<start_character_move "Kirana" -32.6 10 "walk" 0>>
<<wait_for_character_moves>>
<<npc_exit "Kirana">>
<<npc_exit "Lila">>

// Anin is alone.
<<cutscene "fal_fall_offscreen_2">>
// OFFSCREEN ONLY. Same sounds as the prologue, held a beat longer.
// A sound from above, then screams from across the park.
// This time Anin's books hit the floor. She grips the locker door.

Anin: But I... I helped him.

// A crumpled sheet of paper is now on the floor beneath the key hook.
// Make it interactable: Day2_CrumpledPaper (required to end the scene).
// Shows the paper (ActiveIfYarnVariable with Follow Changes).
<<set $d2_paper_dropped to true>>
===

title: Day2_CrumpledPaper
tags: scene3 day2 lockers interactable required
---
// Fal dropped this on his way to take the rooftop key.
// Only the torn end is readable. Do not show the rest anywhere.
<<sfx "crumpled_note_unfold">>
Anin: It's torn. I can only read the end.
Anin: "...not enough."
Anin: His dad's words. Even now.
<<set $d2_found_paper to true>>
<<set $chapter_scene to 4>>
<<hard_reset>>
// TRANSITION → Scene 4: Gap 2
===
